/* Gcd_r: intermediate level of Gcd, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the component BART
   refines.
   Purpose: replace max({dd | ...}) by the facts Euclid's loop establishes: the result is a positive
   common divisor of aa and bb, and every positive common divisor of aa and bb divides it.
   The greatest of the common divisors is thus stated by divisibility, not by order. The one argument
   about order, that a positive number is at least each of its divisors, is made here, away from the
   loop: it gives res : 1..aa and dd <= res, so that res is the max of Gcd. The loop of the next step
   then speaks of divisibility only.
   Same purpose as max_array_r of the max-array demonstration. No variable: nothing is inherited. */
REFINEMENT
    Gcd_r

REFINES
    Gcd

SEES
    Ctx_Gcd

OPERATIONS

    res <-- gcd(aa, bb) =
    PRE
        aa : VAL &
        bb : VAL &
        1 <= aa &
        1 <= bb
    THEN
        res :( res : NAT1 &
               aa mod res = 0 &
               bb mod res = 0 &
               !dd.(dd : NAT1 & aa mod dd = 0 & bb mod dd = 0 => res mod dd = 0) )
    END

END
